'Test timing|After a short unrelated task.|A brief interruption reduces the chance that students are merely repeating the final word in their heads.|During the first presentation.;Before anyone sees the list.;After a full year abroad.',
'Main control|Use the same study time for both groups.|One group must not receive an extra ten minutes simply because its instructions take longer to explain.|Give the picture group twice as long.;Choose different teachers for every word.;Let only one group take notes.',
'Which TWO instructions will the students give?|work individually|Partners could exchange answers and make it unclear whose memory is being measured.|discuss answers with friends;look up every word;write names on public scores',
'Which TWO instructions will the students give?|close the word list|The later task is a recall activity rather than a search for printed answers.',
